26: /**
27:  * Phase 5 T13 — Realtime stream health, recovery, and the drawer's connection
28:  * banner (FR-014, FR-015; AC-014, the messages and list clauses of AC-015,
29:  * the banner clause of AC-037; FR-002's Realtime-recovery trigger).
30:  *
31:  * Real accounts A, B (and C for the account switch), the real app, local
32:  * Supabase and its Realtime. Faults are network shaping (SPEC §15, PLAN D4):
33:  * the browser's offline mode; the T25 per-stream fault harness on A's real
34:  * socket (error, timeout, terminal closure of ONE stream; Presence and the
35:  * other streams untouched); a whole Realtime connection drop by the same
36:  * harness (every socket closed, reconnects refused, then let through); create
37:  * and fence requests failed in transit. AC-014's 3 s "Realtime drop" is both
38:  * required streams failing on the live socket for 3 s: after a whole socket
39:  * drop the socket itself comes back only on the SDK's own reconnect schedule
40:  * (1, 2, 5, 10 s), which the application does not drive, so a 3 s socket drop
41:  * may stay unhealthy for 8 s (the longer socket drop is tested separately). Recovery is never accepted on
42:  * SUBSCRIBED alone: after restore the stream must be joined with its changes
43:  * stream confirmed by the server (waitForReady) and deliver a fresh event
44:  * from B.
45:  *
46:  * Also replaces the deleted mock-based unit test
47:  * __tests__/message-subscription.test.tsx (its retry and identity cases): one
48:  * application retry per failed channel, each on a new topic, with growing
49:  * capped delays; a single joined channel per stream after recovery (retired
50:  * channels left, their late CLOSED ignored: health and banner stay healthy);
51:  * no channel of the previous account after an account switch.
