61: 7. **Medium — a frozen holder still breaks the recovery deadline.**  
62:    **Trigger:** realistic failure: a holder freezes across an outage.  
63:    **Location:** 
[message-outbox.ts:413](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/messaging/outbox/message-outbox.ts:413), 
[message-outbox.ts:717](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/messaging/outbox/message-outbox.ts:717).
64: 
65:    Recovery aborts only requests belonging to the tab handling `online`. An active second tab continues respecting 
the frozen holder’s live 45-second lease. A single pending item can therefore miss the required 10-second recovery 
deadline. TRACK records this at line 473; carrying it to T13 does not waive AC-041 under D11.
66: 
67:    **Smallest fix:** let an active recovering tab supersede pre-outage ownership through a shared recovery epoch 
and server fence.  
68:    **Test:** freeze the holder in the outage test at `cross-tab-outbox.spec.ts:530`, recover only through the 
other active tab, and enforce the same 10-second deadline.
